      <size maxheight='1300' maxwidth='1150' minheight='1300' minwidth='1150' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='77231' id='1' type-v2='text' w='86695' x='696' y='9000'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#050038' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='18'>About this dashboard</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='10'>This dashboard shows information about CTBC Cobranded Cards. The information can be seen in a daily, weekly, month, quarterly or yearly timeframe. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='10'>This dashboard is still </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='10'>WIP</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='10'>. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='14'>Definitions and calculations:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#050038' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='12'>Cards Overview:</run>
              <run>
This tab shows the overall number of binded cards, a trend for when they were binded, and the new customers they helped acquire. 

</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' italic='true'>Active Binded Cards:</run>
              <run italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run>
All cards that have been saved on Foodpanda platform are considered as binded. Once saved, the card can also be deleted thereafter. All cards that are active are also currently saved on the platform, and the cards that are removed will move to &apos;Deleted&apos; category.
</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' italic='true'>New to Platform Customers:</run>
              <run italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run>
If the customer makes the first successful purchase on the platform with the cobrand card, he&apos;s considered in the new-to-platform customer count in this section.  

</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#050038' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='12'>Spend Overview:</run>
              <run>
This tab shows the overview of the spend that&apos;s been made on the card, showing the total card spend over time as well as the spend on Foodpanda app. This tab can be viewed on daily, weekly,(..) level as visible in the date level selector. You can filter the date range you want to use to view the usage and AOV-AOF section and select the metric you want to look at. List of metrics included:
Customers, Transactions, TPV, Refunds, and Refunds Amount

</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' italic='true'>Total Card Spend:</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='10' italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run>
Spend on the CTBC cards as shared in the F1 file from CTBC.
</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' italic='true'>Foodpanda Spend:</run>
              <run italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run>
Spend on the CTBC cards as shared in the F1 file from CTBC, which is spent on Foodpanda (identified using Merchant Identifiers - &apos;000158770142&apos;, &apos;0000158777259&apos;, &apos;000158778001&apos;, &apos;000012019970&apos;). 
</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' italic='true'>Active Customers:</run>
              <run italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run>
Average of customers who have spent in the time period selected. Default is set to show avg. monthly customer. Change the date level selector to see customers on a daily/weekly(..) level.

</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#050038' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='10'>Sections:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' italic='true'>Cobrand Card Usage:</run>
              <run italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run>
This section shows the overall spend on CTBC card - on-FP and off-FP. You can segment this data by binded/non-binded customers to see the split.
</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' italic='true'>Cobrand Card Usage on Foodpanda:</run>
              <run>
This section shows the spend made on cobrand cards on CTBC. This data is sourced from the CTBC reports itself using the MIDs shared.  You can segment this data by Pandapro customers to see the split. Please note that unbinded customers have been marked as non-pro customers in this section. You can also filter this data by the binding status to filter for binded or unbinded customers only.
</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' italic='true'>Foodpanda AOV and AOF:</run>
              <run italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run>
This sections shows the average order value and frequency of the orders made on Foodpanda as shared in the CTBC reports.
</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' italic='true'>Spend Vertical Distribution:</run>
              <run italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run>
This sections which purchase verticals are popular among co-brand card users on Foodpanda. This data shows the percentage of total GMV spent on the vertical. Please note that this information was not available in CTBC reports and has been sourced from Alfred data. Therefore, total GMV might not match the GMV we receive on CTBC reports.
</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' italic='true'>Spend by MCC:</run>
              <run italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run>
This section shows the transactions made on CTBC Co-brand Cards on various MCC. We show the most used MCCs by both - transactions and GMV. You can filter this section by card binding status and pandapro status. We will add the names of these merchant categories once provided by the business team.

</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#050038' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='12'>Cashback Overview:</run>
              <run>
This tab shows the overview of cashbacks that have been processed with their statuses. You can filter this section by Card Binding Status and Pandapro Status.
</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='12' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='8385' id='2' type-v2='text' w='98608' x='696' y='615'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#050038' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='20'>CTBC Co-Brand Card Dashboard</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#707070' fontname='Tableau Regular' fontsize='10'>Update schedule: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#707070' fontname='Tableau Regular' fontsize='10'>Daily</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#707070' fontname='Tableau Regular' fontsize='10'>Point of contact: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#707070' fontname='Tableau Regular' fontsize='10'>Palak Wadhwa - Fintech Wallet Product Analytics Team</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
